WEBVTT

00:02.456 --> 00:05.756
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.860 --> 00:09.092
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.198 --> 00:12.532
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.769 --> 00:15.568
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.873 --> 00:19.001
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.110 --> 00:22.239
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.347 --> 00:24.009
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.117 --> 00:25.744
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.852 --> 00:30.587
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:35.431 --> 00:39.630
<i>We now return to Julia
Louis-Dreyfus in Now It's Just Getting Sad.</i>

00:39.736 --> 00:41.465
<i>Okay, okay, hear me out.</i>

00:41.573 --> 00:45.134
<i>My character is a therapist
living in the city,</i>

00:45.244 --> 00:48.543
<i>but I'm married to an elephant.</i>

00:48.647 --> 00:49.706
<i>Hi, I'm the husband.</i>

00:49.816 --> 00:54.447
<i>Hey, honey. We're going to my parents'
this weekend. Did you pack your trunk?</i>

00:55.656 --> 00:56.919
<i>I don't think I want to go.</i>

00:57.025 --> 00:59.289
<i>- I don't like going to your parents'.
- Why?</i>

00:59.394 --> 01:01.693
<i>Maybe because
your dad's an ivory hunter?</i>

01:01.798 --> 01:04.097
<i>- See? There's a lot going on here.
- Lot going on.</i>

01:04.201 --> 01:06.135
<i>It actually...
It actually gets pretty watchable.</i>

01:08.373 --> 01:11.366
Damn, it's still raining.
Lois, you mind if I go in the house?

01:11.477 --> 01:14.207
Fine, fine, just put the newspaper down.

01:21.256 --> 01:24.715
Hey, Lois, look at this. The church
is holding auditions for a new organist.

01:24.827 --> 01:28.229
Really? Wow. You know,
that sounds like it could be a lot of fun.

01:28.331 --> 01:30.857
Yeah, it's been a while since
you've had the chance to play in public.

01:30.968 --> 01:32.731
Church organist? That's boring.

01:32.837 --> 01:34.169
Why don't you do something
more interesting?

01:34.273 --> 01:36.332
Like when I had that job
feeding the homeless.

01:36.441 --> 01:38.967
That's gonna make you big and strong.

01:39.078 --> 01:44.540
Burping time.
Smells like someone needs to be changed.

01:44.652 --> 01:48.180
When was the last time
you were changed? Seven days ago?

01:48.290 --> 01:51.385
That's one week.
There are seven days in a week.

01:51.994 --> 01:53.895
I love you, filthy hobo.

01:58.836 --> 01:59.826
All right.

02:03.242 --> 02:04.608
Why do you say "organist"
if you don't want...

02:04.711 --> 02:06.338
I don't understand the world anymore.

02:10.718 --> 02:13.483
Here be a jaunty sea shanty
from me boyhood.

02:14.323 --> 02:17.122
<i>You shake me nerves
and you rattle me brain</i>

02:17.427 --> 02:19.828
<i>Too much love drives a man insane</i>

02:20.431 --> 02:21.864
<i>You broke me will</i>

02:21.967 --> 02:23.127
<i>Oh, what a thrill</i>

02:23.234 --> 02:25.795
<i>Goodness gracious, great balls of fire</i>

02:37.286 --> 02:39.516
<i>I know what boys like</i>

02:39.621 --> 02:41.647
<i>I know what guys want</i>

02:42.025 --> 02:44.392
<i>I know what boys like</i>

02:44.662 --> 02:46.357
<i>Boys like</i>

02:46.464 --> 02:48.660
<i>Boys like me</i>

02:48.767 --> 02:51.760
All right, up next is Lois Griffin.

02:52.171 --> 02:56.973
Well, I don't know if I can compete with
the rest of these people, but here goes.

03:01.783 --> 03:05.276
My word, what a fascinating man
this Jesus must've been.

03:05.388 --> 03:06.879
I can just imagine meeting him.

03:37.662 --> 03:39.823
That was beautiful, Mrs. Griffin.

03:39.931 --> 03:41.866
Up next is, Jake Tucker.

03:58.221 --> 04:01.089
Finally. Some of us
have been waiting all evening

04:01.192 --> 04:04.390
for a certain wife to come home
and feed her starving family.

04:04.496 --> 04:07.933
Peter, I told you I was gonna be late.
Couldn't you have handled dinner?

04:08.034 --> 04:09.764
You can't ask me to make dinner, Lois.

04:09.870 --> 04:13.237
That's like asking me to choose between
Sarah Jessica Parker and Kirsten Dunst

04:13.340 --> 04:15.241
in a hot body /weird face contest.

04:15.343 --> 04:18.006
- It can't be done.
- Well, I've got good news.

04:18.114 --> 04:20.480
I'm gonna be the church's new organist.

04:20.583 --> 04:22.108
- Hey, congrats.
- Wow, Mom, that's great.

04:22.219 --> 04:24.119
That means you'll play the organ.

04:24.221 --> 04:28.660
It also means that this family is gonna
start going to church again on Sundays.

04:28.760 --> 04:31.957
Being there today reminded me
of how important religious services are

04:32.065 --> 04:33.760
to the moral fiber of a family.

04:33.867 --> 04:38.362
And lately this family has been lacking
moral fiber. Especially you, Meg.

04:39.273 --> 04:41.299
Meg! What happened to you?

04:41.409 --> 04:44.243
She can't answer you. She can't even talk.

04:44.914 --> 04:48.612
Ever since she started smoking pot,
she just kind of lays there.

04:48.719 --> 04:51.382
It's really sad and a tiny bit funny.

04:51.756 --> 04:54.281
Oh, my God,
I think I'm getting a contact high.

04:54.627 --> 04:55.958
Now I'm messed up, too.

05:00.228 --> 05:04.495
Good morning, everyone.
Please turn to hymn number 387.

05:09.407 --> 05:13.504
<i>God, you are so cool</i>

05:13.612 --> 05:18.073
<i>Although, sometimes
it's, like, what's the deal?</i>

05:18.184 --> 05:22.519
<i>You never answer your cell phone</i>

05:22.623 --> 05:27.618
<i>And your messages are often ambiguous</i>

05:27.729 --> 05:31.427
<i>Amen</i>

05:31.802 --> 05:34.032
A reading from the book of Leviticus.

05:34.137 --> 05:37.938
"Thou shalt not spill thy seed
into thy sock,

05:38.042 --> 05:40.409
"and then cram it
to the bottom of the hamper

05:40.512 --> 05:42.343
"like it's been there a long time. "
The word of the Lord.

05:44.294 --> 05:45.022
- Praise be to God.
- Praise be to God.

05:45.128 --> 05:48.826
Oh, I am so hungry. Hey, look,
they're handing out cookies up there.

05:48.933 --> 05:49.900
Stewie, wait, don't...

05:50.236 --> 05:52.204
Hey, there. Eat up, y'all.

05:52.371 --> 05:55.273
Youse is good churchgoing folk.
Y'all deserve a little treat.

05:55.375 --> 05:56.364
Give me that!

05:56.476 --> 05:59.071
Well, aren't you
an enthusiastic wafer muncher.

05:59.180 --> 06:00.169
What is that, punch?

06:00.281 --> 06:03.581
Oh, don't y'all drink that.
Youse gonna get sick.

06:04.319 --> 06:05.378
Yup.

06:07.090 --> 06:10.458
- That baby just threw up the host!
- That's a sign of the devil!

06:10.561 --> 06:12.496
- Oh, my God, is he possessed?
- He's possessed!

06:12.597 --> 06:14.531
That baby is possessed by Satan!

06:14.633 --> 06:17.068
Calm down, everyone.
He's just a little sick.

06:17.169 --> 06:18.864
I'll take him home. Come on, sweetie.

06:19.338 --> 06:22.934
Sweet, we are out of here. Now I can do
what I planned to do this morning.

06:23.043 --> 06:24.534
Gladiator mice.

06:25.780 --> 06:28.249
Yes! Yes! Die! Die! Die!

06:28.350 --> 06:31.286
I have everything and you have nothing!

06:35.192 --> 06:36.352
What a horrible morning.

06:36.460 --> 06:37.427
You know, all I wanted

06:37.528 --> 06:40.862
was for us to share a simple
Sunday church service as a family.

06:40.966 --> 06:42.901
But I guess that's too much to ask.

06:48.108 --> 06:51.340
Good afternoon, Mrs. Griffin.
We're here to take custody of your baby

06:51.446 --> 06:54.245
so that the good reverend here
can perform an exorcism

06:54.350 --> 06:56.784
and banish the devil from his infant soul.

06:56.886 --> 07:00.550
What? You are not performing
an exorcism on my baby.

07:00.657 --> 07:04.150
Mrs. Griffin, you can give him to us,
or we can take him by force.

07:04.262 --> 07:05.753
- No!
- Don't worry, Lois.

07:05.864 --> 07:08.390
We'll hide in the one place
they can't find us.

07:08.501 --> 07:09.991
In imagination land.

07:10.337 --> 07:13.034
Where you burp where you fart
and you fart where you burp.

07:15.376 --> 07:17.971
Indeed, that's how it happens.

07:24.722 --> 07:25.746
Where're we going?

07:25.856 --> 07:28.917
Who cares? As long as it's away
from those bloody church fanatics.

07:29.027 --> 07:33.488
We're going to Texas. We can stay at my
sister Carol's place until this blows over.

07:33.599 --> 07:37.502
Texas? We're going to Texas
in search of religious tolerance?

07:37.604 --> 07:40.836
That's gonna be like trying to get
Sneakers O'Toole to take his sneakers off.

07:41.142 --> 07:45.011
<i>I'm not taking my sneakers off
I'm Sneakers O'Toole</i>

07:45.180 --> 07:46.705
Hey, take those sneakers off.

07:46.816 --> 07:48.249
- No!
- Take them off, I said!

07:48.351 --> 07:49.341
No!

07:50.021 --> 07:53.924
Let him go. We'll never catch him.
Not in these shoes.

07:54.026 --> 07:56.460
<i>I didn't take my sneakers off
I'm still Sneakers O'Toole</i>

08:18.411 --> 08:19.640
Holy crap!

08:20.213 --> 08:23.342
You marry Billy Joel,
it's gonna happen one way or another.

08:23.651 --> 08:26.279
- Good evening. I'm Tom Tucker.
- And I'm Diane Simmons.

08:26.388 --> 08:29.152
Authorities are on the lookout
for one-year-old Stewie Griffin,

08:29.258 --> 08:32.387
a Quahog infant who is believed
to be possessed by Satan.

08:32.495 --> 08:34.726
A substantial reward is being offered for
any information leading to his capture.

08:36.677 --> 08:40.444
In other pseudo-scientific news, a local
man claims to have spotted Bigfoot.

08:40.549 --> 08:42.142
We've got the exclusive interview.

08:42.385 --> 08:45.844
I was about to bone my girlfriend,
out at the lake,

08:45.956 --> 08:50.257
but suddenly, she yelled,
so I looked up and it was Bigfoot.

08:50.361 --> 08:53.331
- So, what happened next?
- Then, I went back to bone her,

08:53.432 --> 08:58.302
but the mosquitoes were going crazy
and she said there was no way.

09:00.775 --> 09:04.041
All right, get your snacks,
and hurry out, you guys.

09:04.379 --> 09:06.370
There, look, they have Chunky bars.

09:06.481 --> 09:10.350
What a God-awful mess those things are.
Chocolate with raisins in it.

09:10.453 --> 09:13.514
Yeah. Yeah, that's what kids
want with their chocolate, fruit.

09:13.624 --> 09:16.423
Why don't you put sunflower seeds
in the Ding Dongs while you're at it?

09:16.528 --> 09:17.790
Is that part of your stand-up act?

09:17.896 --> 09:19.626
- I don't know. Did you like it?
- I wouldn't open with it.

09:23.036 --> 09:25.596
Pardon me, sir.
We're trying to locate a possessed child.

09:25.706 --> 09:27.174
Have you seen anyone who looks like this?

09:27.275 --> 09:29.710
Yeah, that's my son.
He's actually in the Mini Mart right now.

09:29.812 --> 09:30.870
He'll be out in a second.

09:32.047 --> 09:33.640
I mean, I mean, no.
No, never seen him before.

09:33.750 --> 09:34.739
Hmm...

09:34.851 --> 09:36.113
What was that first thing you said?

09:36.219 --> 09:38.586
Oh, I was just saying
that baby in the picture is my son.

09:38.689 --> 09:40.715
He's traveling with us.
He's part of our family.

09:40.826 --> 09:43.420
We're trying to avoid being found
by police like you.

09:43.795 --> 09:47.755
I mean, I was just remarking
what a nice tie you have on.

09:47.867 --> 09:50.462
I love this tie.

09:50.571 --> 09:52.130
All right, you folks take care now.

09:53.808 --> 09:55.469
Did you hear that cashier's accent?

09:55.578 --> 09:58.138
" Would you like
some change please, for you?"

09:58.247 --> 10:00.944
You know, if it weren't for 9/11,
those guys would be adorable.

10:01.051 --> 10:02.643
Oh, my God, look!

10:03.888 --> 10:05.185
Quick, into the bathroom!

10:06.524 --> 10:08.857
We're gonna have to come up with a way
to change your appearance.

10:08.961 --> 10:11.192
Well, I could disguise myself
as Britney Spears.

10:11.297 --> 10:13.925
I'm already standing in urine,
and I hate the person I'm with.

10:14.034 --> 10:16.595
Now, let's see, there's got to be
something in here we can use.

10:25.014 --> 10:28.678
Boy, that was a close one back there.
Way to think on your feet, Brian.

10:28.786 --> 10:31.153
Well, we got lucky.
How you holding up, Stewie?

10:31.256 --> 10:32.484
Um...

10:32.825 --> 10:34.850
I feel right, Brian. I feel right.

10:44.410 --> 10:46.776
Are you sure Aunt Carol won't mind
us using her house?

10:46.879 --> 10:49.678
She won't care, Chris.
She's off on her ninth honeymoon.

10:51.084 --> 10:53.349
When will it work for her?

10:54.288 --> 10:56.450
Howdy, new neighbors.
Pleased to welcome you.

10:56.558 --> 10:59.027
We're the Lynches. We live next door.

10:59.129 --> 11:01.689
Nice to meet you. We're the Griffins.

11:01.798 --> 11:05.235
Nellie here is a homemaker,
and I'm a queer chaser and beater.

11:05.336 --> 11:07.805
Lois, I'm not sure
this is the right place for us.

11:07.906 --> 11:12.241
These Texans are socially backward and
politically, they're all stubborn as a mule.

11:12.578 --> 11:15.377
<i>No, sorry,
Kevin Bacon wasn't in Footloose.</i>

11:15.682 --> 11:18.208
- What? Of course he was.
- No, he wasn't. You lose.

11:18.319 --> 11:20.787
- Of course he was. He was the star.
- No, you're wrong. Look it up.

11:20.889 --> 11:22.551
I don't have to look it up.
It's common knowledge.

11:22.658 --> 11:23.955
- He was on the cover of...
- No, no, no.

11:24.059 --> 11:25.618
<i>...People magazine when the movie...
- No, no.</i>

11:25.729 --> 11:26.718
- Everyone knows...
- No, no.

11:26.830 --> 11:28.297
<i>...Kevin Bacon was the star of Footloose.
- No, no, no!</i>

11:28.398 --> 11:30.492
- It was a huge movie. He was the lead.
- No, no, no, no!

11:30.601 --> 11:31.795
No, no, no...

11:37.710 --> 11:39.405
Look what the Lynches gave us.

11:39.512 --> 11:43.108
<i>A needlepoint of Chuck Norris
from Walker, Texas Ranger.</i>

11:43.217 --> 11:45.186
You know, they say
Chuck Norris is so tough,

11:45.287 --> 11:47.313
there's no chin under his beard.

11:47.423 --> 11:50.483
- There is only another fist.
- That's ridiculous.

11:51.061 --> 11:52.653
Chuck Norris?

11:53.831 --> 11:57.427
You know, this place may be the upside
to everything that's happened.

11:57.535 --> 12:01.028
The people are kind and generous.
They seem wholesome and moral,

12:01.140 --> 12:03.939
exactly the kind of influence
this family needs.

12:04.044 --> 12:07.276
Lois, we're living in a red state
with a bunch of right-wing nut jobs.

12:07.381 --> 12:11.614
Hey, Chris, check out my belt buckle.
It says, "Everything's bigger in Texas. "

12:13.088 --> 12:16.286
Belts are a great way to express opinions.

12:18.462 --> 12:21.830
<i>This is Channel Five News,
Texas, with Duke Dillon.</i>

12:21.933 --> 12:24.094
<i>Howdy, Texas, I'm Duke Dillon.</i>

12:24.202 --> 12:27.263
<i>At the top of the news tonight,
authorities have called off their pursuit</i>

12:27.373 --> 12:30.969
<i>of a fugitive Rhode Island baby who was
thought to be possessed by the devil.</i>

12:31.078 --> 12:32.637
Oh, thank God.

12:32.747 --> 12:35.842
<i>This turn of events came
after Vatican scientists announced today</i>

12:35.951 --> 12:38.784
<i>that the devil is not the greatest threat
to salvation</i>

12:38.888 --> 12:41.858
<i>due to last week's discovery
of the super devil.</i>

12:41.958 --> 12:43.824
<i>Religion reporter Dallas Houston
has the story.</i>

12:43.928 --> 12:44.895
<i>Thanks, Duke.</i>

12:44.996 --> 12:47.761
<i>Well, let me try to give you a clear picture
of what we're dealing with here.</i>

12:47.866 --> 12:50.734
<i>Here's a photo of the devil,
and here's the super devil.</i>

12:50.837 --> 12:53.397
<i>Now, as you can see,
there are some significant differences.</i>

12:53.506 --> 12:56.169
<i>The super devil is at least 6 inches taller.</i>

12:56.277 --> 12:57.870
<i>He has a flying motorcycle</i>

12:57.979 --> 13:01.507
<i>and a jar of marmalade that we believe
forces you to commit adultery.</i>

13:01.617 --> 13:02.709
<i>Thanks a lot, Dallas.</i>

13:02.818 --> 13:05.344
<i>Looks like we've all got
something new to be afraid of.</i>

13:05.589 --> 13:09.321
Everyone, it's over.
We can go back to Quahog.

13:12.798 --> 13:14.823
Hey, Lois, did you say something?

13:14.934 --> 13:17.597
Oh, just that I think
you're gonna love this cake.

13:17.704 --> 13:21.106
None for me, thanks.
It's gonna go straight to my vagina.

13:21.208 --> 13:23.574
That's what girls worry about, right?
Having big vaginas?

13:28.184 --> 13:30.175
Dad, why aren't you taking the car?

13:30.286 --> 13:32.687
Chris, we're in Texas now.
If I'm not riding a horse,

13:32.790 --> 13:35.783
I'm gonna stick out like a straight guy
in a figure skating competition.

13:38.597 --> 13:40.862
Boo-ya! Triple salchow in your face!

13:40.967 --> 13:43.027
Hey, you want this?
Huh? You want some of this?

13:43.136 --> 13:46.163
Oh, man, look at your rack.
I'd motorboat that.

13:46.341 --> 13:50.278
I'd motorboat the hell out of it.
Right after this layback spin.

13:54.751 --> 13:56.150
Bottle of Jack Daniel's, please.

13:56.252 --> 13:58.915
- Here you go.
- Thanks. What's this?

13:59.023 --> 14:01.652
That's your gun.
Buy some liquor, get a free gun.

14:01.760 --> 14:04.160
Is that, like,
a special you have on now or something?

14:04.262 --> 14:07.232
Nope, Texas state law.
You have a nice day now.

14:07.333 --> 14:08.494
State law?

14:08.602 --> 14:11.469
God, this place officially sucks
worse than the WNBA.

14:13.074 --> 14:15.839
And at the top of the second half,
it's 16 to 9.

14:15.945 --> 14:17.640
Easton leads the scoring with four.

14:17.747 --> 14:20.911
And that's why
she commands $7,000 a year.

14:21.018 --> 14:23.283
These gals sure do make it look difficult.

14:23.388 --> 14:26.915
But is having this minor skill
worth being so unattractive?

14:27.026 --> 14:29.017
That's for the fan to decide.

14:29.128 --> 14:30.152
Yay!

14:34.969 --> 14:35.958
Huh.

14:36.937 --> 14:38.929
That was kind of cool.

14:47.084 --> 14:49.018
Been a long day, Lois. Long day.

14:49.119 --> 14:52.681
Peter, what the hell?
You can't bring that horse into our bed!

14:52.791 --> 14:55.727
Lois, I cannot believe
you would ban the horse from our bed.

14:55.828 --> 14:57.729
He is a graceful, majestic creature

14:57.831 --> 15:00.528
who is a part of this family
and only wants your love and respect.

15:00.635 --> 15:02.125
The horse may have pooped in the bed.

15:05.574 --> 15:09.204
I hereby call this meeting
of the Texas Youth Club to order.

15:09.312 --> 15:13.545
First, I'd like to welcome our
two newcomers, Chris and Meg Griffin.

15:13.651 --> 15:16.746
Wow, this is the coolest club
I've ever been in.

15:16.888 --> 15:19.153
Well, you're not quite in the club yet.

15:19.258 --> 15:22.056
- You got to pass the initiation.
- What do we have to do?

15:22.161 --> 15:24.096
You got to sneak onto the Crawford Ranch

15:24.198 --> 15:26.690
and steal a pair of
George Bush's underwear.

15:26.801 --> 15:30.898
And then bring it back here,
so we can bask in its Bushy goodness.

15:31.006 --> 15:34.670
Boy, that's even kinkier than the porn
they make for senior citizens.

15:36.480 --> 15:38.073
Can I help you, Edward?

15:38.182 --> 15:40.912
Yeah, I'm here for the early bird special.

15:42.121 --> 15:44.885
- Are those new slacks?
- What's that now?

15:44.990 --> 15:49.986
- Are those new slacks?
- I got these on special at Caldor.

15:50.097 --> 15:52.532
- Who drove you there?
- My nephew.

15:52.634 --> 15:53.601
Oh!

15:53.702 --> 15:55.260
That was nice of him.

15:55.370 --> 15:57.168
I forgot why I came over.

15:58.274 --> 16:00.243
Are those new slacks?

16:05.216 --> 16:06.945
What is this?
What the hell are we doing here?

16:07.051 --> 16:09.282
Welcome to your first
toddler pageant, Stewie.

16:09.388 --> 16:10.377
It's what you do when you're in Texas.

16:12.003 --> 16:15.963
Oh, lovely. A first-class ticket to a
semen-covered death in the basement.

16:16.074 --> 16:17.871
Why don't you meet the other contestants
while I go register you?

16:19.822 --> 16:22.724
Hello, I'm Stephanie Griffin.

16:22.859 --> 16:24.884
- Hi, Stephanie.
- What's your talent?

16:24.994 --> 16:29.933
I sing, I do gymnastics, and I can play
seven instruments at the same time.

16:30.702 --> 16:32.966
You could be a threat to me. Chuck.

16:37.344 --> 16:39.744
There it is. The Crawford Ranch.

16:39.847 --> 16:42.009
I can't believe we're actually doing this.

16:42.116 --> 16:44.243
What a bonding adventure
for the two of us.

16:44.352 --> 16:48.290
Settle down, Meg. Okay, I see
old man Cheney guarding the place.

16:50.193 --> 16:52.219
18% approval ratings.

16:54.198 --> 16:56.963
I'll give you 18% of my foot in your ass.

16:59.472 --> 17:02.532
I'd like you to meet
my daughter's husband, Michael.

17:16.693 --> 17:19.356
Wow, look how organized he is.

17:19.464 --> 17:23.902
He's already got his sugar cut up into neat
little lines for his breakfast tomorrow.

17:24.003 --> 17:26.063
And a razor blade to shave.

17:27.173 --> 17:28.572
Wow, look at this.

17:28.675 --> 17:31.543
I can't believe Mrs. Bush kept
all these Planned Parenthood receipts.

17:31.646 --> 17:32.704
Holy cow!

17:32.813 --> 17:35.840
She's been scraped more times
than a fisherman's knuckle.

17:35.951 --> 17:37.510
Hey! What are you kids doing here?

17:37.620 --> 17:40.647
You tell Javier to back off.
I'll have his money by next week.

17:40.758 --> 17:42.248
- What?
- Never mind.

17:42.359 --> 17:46.057
Hey, you guys wanna see something?
Grab a beer and follow me.

17:47.332 --> 17:50.166
See this car?
I restored it myself this summer.

17:50.269 --> 17:52.864
I was here for 12 weeks.
I had to do something.

17:52.973 --> 17:55.943
But along the way,
I learned about honesty, integrity

17:56.044 --> 17:59.071
and cold-filtered Miller Genuine Draft.

18:00.816 --> 18:02.944
That's an adult beverage right there.

18:03.053 --> 18:04.543
You understand
what I'm trying to say to you?

18:04.654 --> 18:06.816
Yes, but I have just one question.

18:06.924 --> 18:09.017
Can I borrow your underpants
for 10 minutes?

18:19.974 --> 18:21.840
Hello? Oh, hi, Jillian.

18:21.943 --> 18:24.411
<i>Brian, I'm reading TV Guide.</i>

18:24.512 --> 18:28.472
Can you explain how these
"cheers" and "jeers" work again?

18:28.584 --> 18:32.647
Well, the "cheers" is when they generally
approve of something on television,

18:32.757 --> 18:36.353
and "jeers" is when
they find some sort of fault with it.

18:37.196 --> 18:39.630
See, yeah, I'm not quite...

18:39.732 --> 18:43.032
We can't do this over the phone.
You're gonna have to come over.

18:43.136 --> 18:44.764
I can't come over. We're still on the run,

18:44.872 --> 18:46.567
because the town thinks
Stewie's possessed.

18:46.674 --> 18:50.702
No, they don't. Didn't you hear?
They stopped chasing you weeks ago.

18:50.812 --> 18:54.305
- What? I have to go.
- Wait, wait, I have another question.

18:54.417 --> 18:56.147
How do I know if I'm Jewish?

18:56.253 --> 18:57.311
- Are you Jewish?
- No.

18:57.421 --> 18:58.980
- There you go, sport.
- Thank you.

19:00.425 --> 19:02.519
Hey, guys, thanks so much
for inviting me out today.

19:02.628 --> 19:04.596
I'm psyched to brand my first cow.

19:04.697 --> 19:07.861
Here you are, Peter.
All fired up and ready to go.

19:12.740 --> 19:17.372
Yes! Yes! Hang on a second.

19:25.824 --> 19:28.157
Man, Texas is great. Back where I'm from,

19:28.261 --> 19:31.230
a retarded guy
could never have this much fun.

19:31.731 --> 19:35.566
- What'd you just say?
- What? Technically, I'm retarded.

19:36.071 --> 19:38.198
Fellas, fellas, can't we talk this over?

19:38.306 --> 19:42.971
Talking is for terrorists and blacks.
In Texas, we execute the retarded!

19:43.146 --> 19:45.614
Oh, my God. So, this is how it ends?

19:45.715 --> 19:49.243
I always thought I'd die having to
sit through the Canadian Film Festival.

19:49.353 --> 19:53.654
<i>I don't wish to cause you any harm,
and I won't. The end.</i>

20:04.873 --> 20:08.275
- Horsey, you saved my life.
- No problem, Peter.

20:08.377 --> 20:11.506
- Glad to help out.
- Wow, Gilbert Gottfried.

20:11.615 --> 20:13.481
- That's right!
- Awesome.

20:17.857 --> 20:22.295
Now, the final contestant for
our talent portion of the competition,

20:22.395 --> 20:25.490
- Stephanie Griffin.
- Thank you, thank you.

20:25.600 --> 20:28.035
Hey, what's the deal
with Chunky bars, huh?

20:28.137 --> 20:30.002
Chocolate with raisins in it.

20:30.105 --> 20:33.007
Yeah, that's what kids want
with their chocolate, fruit.

20:35.011 --> 20:36.343
Wow, that bit's killing.

20:36.447 --> 20:38.608
Hey, Lois, great news.
We can go back to Quahog.

20:38.716 --> 20:39.809
Yeah, I know, Brian.

20:40.986 --> 20:42.214
We're about to see if Stewie won.

20:42.320 --> 20:45.085
Wait a minute, you know?
How long have you known?

20:45.191 --> 20:47.717
- A few weeks. Who cares?
- Wait a minute. You...

20:47.828 --> 20:51.162
You've known for weeks and you've been
lying about having to stay here?

20:51.266 --> 20:52.665
Brian, don't you see?

20:52.767 --> 20:55.828
This is a wholesome community
with real values.

20:55.938 --> 20:58.271
And our first runner-up is...

20:59.476 --> 21:01.411
Miss Dixie-Ann Thomas,

21:01.512 --> 21:07.418
which means that Miss Stephanie Griffin
is our new Little Miss Texas!

21:11.057 --> 21:13.652
Oh! Oh, my God!
Oh, I never expected this!

21:13.761 --> 21:16.196
Oh, I'm so, so honored!

21:18.433 --> 21:21.665
- Hey! That's not a girl!
- It's Enrico Palazzo!

21:21.771 --> 21:24.172
No, it's not!
It's one of them queerosexuals!

21:24.274 --> 21:25.571
Get him!

21:31.183 --> 21:32.707
Quick, get on!

21:41.028 --> 21:43.793
- Thank you for all your help.
- My pleasure, Peter.

21:43.899 --> 21:46.164
- Any time.
- Oh, fantastic.

21:46.269 --> 21:49.295
- Hey, do you still do stand-up?
- I do. I'm still touring.

21:49.405 --> 21:51.397
- Oh, wow, can we get tickets?
- Absolutely.

21:51.508 --> 21:55.104
- I'm in Atlanta next week.
- Great. Oh, well, this will be fun.

22:03.557 --> 22:05.458
It is so good to be home.

22:05.560 --> 22:09.361
You know, I wanted us to live in a place
with real family values.

22:09.465 --> 22:12.993
But values don't come from where you live
or who your friends are.

22:13.103 --> 22:15.937
They come from inside,
from your own beliefs.

22:16.040 --> 22:19.168
I agree, Lois. Like for instance,
if you're watching a TV show

22:19.278 --> 22:22.770
and you decide to take your values
from that, you're an idiot.

22:22.881 --> 22:26.613
Maybe you should take responsibility
for what values your kids are getting.

22:26.720 --> 22:29.951
Maybe you shouldn't be letting your kids
watch certain shows in the first place

22:30.057 --> 22:34.428
if you have such a big problem with them,
instead of blaming the shows themselves.

22:35.931 --> 22:36.989
Yeah.

22:36.990 --> 23:37.990
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru